   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Eco Hub Project- ALMA Tofo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Eco Hub project for ALMA was created to provide the first waste innovation space in Mozambique, located at the headquarters of ALMA in Tofo, Inhambane Province.
ALMA provides waste management services for the community of Tofo under a contract with the Inhambane Municipality, who is not able to provide these services due to the remote location of Tofo, one of the largest tourism destinations in the Country with close to 100 lodges, restaurants, and diving centers, which generate considerable amounts of waste, specifically plastic (from water bottles and food containers), glass (from beverages), paper (from packaging) and metal (from cans</narrative>
  </description>
